cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ChemFlow, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "ChemFlow: An Auditable Workflow for Docking-Based Virtual Screening with Redocking Validation and Chemometric Analysis"
abstract: >-
  ChemFlow is an open-source Python workflow that integrates ligand and receptor preparation, AutoDock Vina
  docking with seeded replicates, redocking validation by in-place heavy-atom RMSD, interaction similarity to
  the native ligand, ADMET and descriptor summaries, chemometric analysis (PCA, hierarchical clustering) and an
  optional GC-MS module, behind a command line, a web interface and a Python library.
type: software
version: 3.1.0
authors:
  - family-names: Azis
    given-names: Arif Maulana
    email: titandigitalsoft@gmail.com
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Arifmaulanaazis/chemflow"
url: "https://github.com/Arifmaulanaazis/chemflow"
keywords:
  - molecular docking
  - virtual screening
  - AutoDock Vina
  - redocking validation
  - chemometrics
  - GC-MS
